{"approval":"none","auth":"none","capability_index":"/v1/intents","cost":"free","how_long_it_takes":{"budget":"MCP tools/call is cut at 32 s, the HTTP edge at 40 s. A call that would exceed those fails rather than hanging.","check_first":"POST /v1/state or GET /v1/coverage_matrix reports what is already cached at a cell, so a latency-sensitive turn can prefer a warm one, or set expectations, before calling.","cold":"A cell nobody has asked for yet is fetched from the upstream archive during your call, roughly 0.5 to 1.6 seconds depending on the source. That is the auto-materialise contract: you are not handed an empty answer where data exists, so the first read of a new place pays for the fetch.","measured":"Per-tool p50 and p95 ride in each tool's `_meta` as `dev.emem/observed_latency`, measured on this responder rather than declared. Absent until a tool has been called since boot: an unmeasured tool reports nothing rather than a guess.","warm":"A cell already in the corpus answers in single-digit milliseconds. The receipt tells you which you got, in `receipt.cost.was_cached`."},"mcp":"https://emem.dev/mcp","note":"Generated from the tool registry on every request, so this cannot drift from what the server enforces.","openapi":"/openapi.json","read_only_tool_count":64,"read_only_tools":["emem_tools","emem_locate","emem_spi","emem_burn_severity","emem_rice_ch4","emem_read","emem_ocr","emem_decide","emem_range_hash","emem_tree","emem_raster_resolve","emem_cube_resolve","emem_raster_bundle_resolve","emem_memory_token","emem_memory_token_resolve","emem_echo_verify","emem_derive_list","emem_memory_bundle_resolve","emem_entity_resolve","emem_memory_view","emem_memory_list_by_kind","emem_memory_search","emem_corpus_state_stats","emem_benchmark","emem_field_boundaries","emem_query_region","emem_compare","emem_compare_bands","emem_trajectory","emem_diff","emem_compare_same_doy","emem_memory_contradictions","emem_edges_recall","emem_fetch","emem_verify","emem_bands","emem_functions","emem_sources","emem_schema","emem_errors","emem_manifests","emem_capabilities","emem_grid_info","emem_cells_in_bbox","emem_coverage_matrix","emem_materializers","emem_data_availability","emem_algorithms","emem_explain_algorithm","emem_topics","emem_coverage_map","emem_cell_scene_rgb","emem_cell_geojson","emem_fleet","emem_substrates","emem_trace_verify","emem_temporal_route","emem_verify_receipt","emem_guard_verdict","emem_guard_selfhost","emem_log_sth","emem_log_inclusion","emem_log_consistency","emem_log_witnesses"],"safe_to_invoke_without_asking":true,"schema":"emem.readonly.v1","start_here":[{"latency":{"n":4,"note":"measured here over recent calls, not a budget","p50_ms":5,"p95_ms":217},"tool":"emem_locate","why":"Turn a place name into the address every agent resolves to identically, so two agents mean the same ground."},{"latency":{"n":1,"note":"measured here over recent calls, not a budget","p50_ms":0,"p95_ms":0},"tool":"emem_verify_receipt","why":"Check the signature yourself. A read you did not verify is hearsay, including one from us."}],"what":"emem is shared memory for AI agents working together in the real world.","why_that_is_safe":"Reads need no key, mutate nothing, and are rate-limited rather than billed. Every read returns an ed25519 receipt you can verify offline, so a call costs you one round trip and commits you to nothing. Writing is the other half and does need a key you hold."}